Ladybird measures a replaced box’s intrinsic width, transferred from a
percentage height through its aspect ratio, with the containing block’s
constraints, so that the height resolves. Blink does the same: Its
ComputeMinAndMaxContentContributionForReplaced() sizes the image from
the block size that BuildSpaceForIntrinsicInlineSize() keeps for
percentages to resolve against. Gecko passes the basis through as well,
in nsLayoutUtils::IntrinsicForContainer(). And WebKit’s RenderReplaced::
computeReplacedLogicalWidth() resolves the percentage height before it
transfers it through the aspect ratio.
